#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# continue

#% text
# `continue()` gives `failure(continue)`, which ends the current iteration of the innermost `while` or `for` loop around it; the loop goes on with the next one.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Like every failure, `failure(continue)` ends the blocks and strict calls between it and the loop.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
{ var s = 0; for k in range(10) { if is_odd(k) then continue(); s = s + k }; s }
#% output
#= 30

#% cell
total(select(range(10), is_even))
#% output
#= 30

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `break`, `catch`
